{"chunk_id":"7fa943","wall_time_seconds":0.577697958,"exit_code":0,"original_token_count":1187,"output":"{"date":"2026-08-14T14:18:15Z","message":"refactor(hooks)!: remove local_dev mode\n\nLocal-dev mode pointed installed hooks at `scripts/entire-dev`, a launcher\ninside the working tree that compiled and ran the checked-out source. It was\nread from the *committed* `.entire/settings.json` (settings.go merged\n`local_dev` from the project scope, and strategy/common.go regenerated the git\nhook from it), so any repository could commit `\"local_dev\": true` and have\n`entire enable` install hooks that execute that repository's own code. A branch\ncheckout could then swap what ran. This repo shipped exactly that: `local_dev:\ntrue` was tracked, and all six committed agent configs invoked the launcher.\n\nHooks now always name the `entire` binary. Removed the `--local-dev` flags\n(including the non-hidden one on `entire agent add`), `EnableOptions.LocalDev`,\nthe `localDev` parameter from `Agent.InstallHooks` across all nine agents and\nthe external-agent protocol, the claude-code local-dev SessionEnd timeout, and\nthe launcher script.\n\n`EntireSettings.LocalDev` stays as a documented no-op: the loaders use\nDisallowUnknownFields, so deleting the field would make every existing settings\nfile containing `local_dev` a hard parse error. It is not merged from overrides\nand nothing reads it, matching the `Strategy` precedent.\n\nRemoving the feature is not enough to disarm existing installs, so this also\nfixes how hooks written by older versions get replaced:\n\n- `isGitHookInstalledInHooksDir` only looked for the Entire marker, which a\n  legacy hook still carries. It therefore read as installed forever and\n  EnsureSetup never reinstalled it — while the script it invoked no longer\n  existed. Repo-relative prefixes got no availability guard and pre-push\n  deliberately propagates exit codes, so that state rejects `git push`. A hook\n  naming the legacy launcher now counts as not installed.\n- claudecode, factoryaidroid and copilotcli only dropped Entire hooks under\n  `--force`, so a plain enable added the current hook beside the legacy one and\n  both fired. cursor and codex returned early whenever the current command was\n  present, leaving a legacy hook next to it. Stale hooks are now dropped on\n  every install, through one shared `agent.DropStaleManagedHooks` primitive\n  rather than six per-agent re-derivations (`dupl` cannot see duplication across\n  packages, which is how the two divergent copies survived).\n- geminicli's idempotency check sampled only SessionStart, so a stale hook on\n  any of the other ten types survived every non-force install.\n- The write now happens when only a drop occurred: a config can hold both a\n  stale and a current hook, where nothing needs adding.\n- Every hook prefix is guarded by an existence test. The unguarded path existed\n  only for the repo-relative launcher, and was still reachable for unusual\n  absolute paths — exactly where losing the guard hurts most.\n\nRegenerates this repo's six committed agent configs through the real install\npath. The pi extension had also drifted far enough to be missing the\nENTIRE_PI_NESTED subagent guard that was already in its template, so\n`testutil.AssertCommittedDogfoodFile` and `AssertCommittedDogfoodConfigStable`\nnow fail in CI on drift instead of waiting for someone to notice.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M00A6KK7GC43YE6DT3WX5FWN","sha":"a9a676e7959784f76bb5dcde2ab1fb09b33fbfd3"}
